    "sections": [
      {
        "label": "1st quarter",
        "score": "NY 27, BOS 26",
        "text": "A scrappy start. Mitchell Robinson, facing the Knicks team he spent his first eight seasons with, ran into early foul trouble, and New York led 27–26 after one."
      },
      {
        "label": "2nd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 50, NY 49",
        "text": "The first half went back and forth (the game had 12 lead changes and four ties), and Boston took a 50–49 lead into the break. Neemias Queta was the only Celtic to attempt a free throw in the half."
      },
      {
        "label": "3rd quarter",
        "score": "BOS 83, NY 73",
        "text": "Boston won the quarter 33–24 to lead by 10 going into the fourth. Jayson Tatum, who scored 25 of his 36 after halftime, got to the line with 3:21 left in the third, the first Celtic other than Queta to shoot a free throw."
      },
      {
        "label": "4th quarter",
        "score": "Final: BOS 107, NY 103",
        "text": "Boston led by as many as 12 (91–79) before a 12–3 Knicks run cut it to 94–91 on a Karl-Anthony Towns putback dunk. Josh Hart's three made it 99–96, and a Queta turnover led to a Jalen Brunson floater for 99–98. Tatum answered with a 19-footer (101–98) and, after a Towns offensive foul, a deep corner two for 103–98 with 49 seconds left; OG Anunoby's free throws made it 103–100 before Tatum's three from the left wing over Towns sealed it."
      }
    ],
